This is a known breaking change. Android 15 (API 35) — which .NET 10 MAUI targets — enforces **edge-to-edge** rendering, making `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE` a no-op.

## Fix: Use Window Insets

Replace `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` with inset-based padding in your `MainActivity`:

```csharp
// Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new InsetsListener());
}

private class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var systemBarInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

        // Use the larger of IME or system bar bottom padding
        int bottomPadding = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemBarInsets.Bottom);
        v.SetPadding(systemBarInsets.Left, systemBarInsets.Top, systemBarInsets.Right, bottomPadding);

        return insets;
    }
}
```

Then **remove** any old resize config:

```diff
- App.Current.On<Microsoft.Maui.Controls.PlatformConfiguration.Android>()
-     .UseWindowSoftInputModeAdjust(WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize);
```

## Why this works

Edge-to-edge means your app draws behind the keyboard. The `Ime()` inset tells you the keyboard height, so you apply it as bottom padding — the layout shifts up naturally.

## Alternative: MAUI's built-in auto-scroll

MAUI has `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` enabled by default, which scrolls focused `Entry`/`Editor` views into view. If it's not working for your layout, you can ensure it's active:

```csharp
// In MauiProgram.cs — this is the default, but be explicit:
builder.ConfigureMauiHandlers(handlers =>
{
    Microsoft.Maui.Platform.KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Connect(true);
});
```

The insets approach gives you full control and is the recommended long-term fix for bottom-pinned input bars.
